    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Phishing — Delivered LNK written to Desktop", "technique": "T1204.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-11-04 09:12:33 CET, Wazuh FIM (File Integrity Monitoring) fired rule 92810 'FIM: LNK file on Desktop' on host WIN-FINANCE-07 (10.20.14.107). The new file C:\\Users\\mcharpentier\\Desktop\\Q4_Bonus.pdf.lnk appeared on the Desktop of user mcharpentier — the double extension (.pdf.lnk) masquerades as a PDF document to trick the user into double-clicking it. The LNK file was created via WScript.Shell COM object, consistent with delivery via a macro-enabled Office document or a script dropped by a spearphishing e-mail attachment opened earlier. The MOTW (Mark-of-the-Web) Zone.Identifier ADS on the file confirms it originated from the internet (ZoneId=3).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh FIM rule 52103 fired on syscheck.path=C:\\Users\\mcharpentier\\Desktop\\Q4_Bonus.pdf.lnk with syscheck.event=added. The double extension + MOTW ZoneId=3 signature is a canonical spearphishing LNK delivery indicator (MITRE T1204.002).", "first_seen": "2026-11-04T09:12:33+0100"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Execution — User Double-Clicks LNK, shell32.dll/explorer.exe Spawns PowerShell", "technique": "T1204.002 + T1059.001", "what_happened": "At 09:14:17 CET, Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Create) fired on WIN-FINANCE-07. explorer.exe (parentImage) invoked powershell.exe (image) with a hidden, non-interactive, encoded command via the LNK Target field. The commandLine contained -WindowStyle Hidden -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -EncodedCommand, concealing the payload from casual inspection. The process was created under the security context of mcharpentier (NT AUTHORITY context confirms shell32.dll resolved the LNK Target and launched powershell.exe as the logged-on user). Wazuh rule 92810 'LNK file execution from Desktop (user execution)' fired simultaneously.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1: data.win.eventdata.parentImage=C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe + data.win.eventdata.image=C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe + data.win.eventdata.commandLine contains -EncodedCommand. The parent-child pair (explorer.exe → powershell.exe) with EncodedCommand is the canonical double-click-LNK-spawns-hidden-PS signature.", "first_seen": "2026-11-04T09:14:17+0100"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Execution — PowerShell Spawns cmd.exe Child (Decoded Stage)", "technique": "T1059.003", "what_happened": "At 09:14:19 CET, 2 seconds after the PowerShell launch, Sysmon EID 1 fired again on WIN-FINANCE-07: powershell.exe (parentImage) spawned cmd.exe (image) with commandLine 'cmd.exe /c whoami & hostname & ipconfig /all'. This is the decoded first-stage recon payload hidden inside the LNK's EncodedCommand. The three chained commands (whoami, hostname, ipconfig /all) are the canonical attacker post-execution orientation fingerprint — identical to automated dropper scaffolding that beacons results back to C2.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1: data.win.eventdata.parentImage=C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe + data.win.eventdata.image=C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe + data.win.eventdata.commandLine='cmd.exe /c whoami & hostname & ipconfig /all'. The 2-second parent-child gap (automated, not human-typed) + recon trio confirms scripted payload execution.", "first_seen": "2026-11-04T09:14:19+0100"}
